### Example API requests for the Client Management System.
### IntelliJ IDEA can run these with the green arrow next to each request
### (HTTP Client). Start the application first. Replace the IDs with real ones.

### Health check (is MongoDB reachable?)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/health

### Create a client (status becomes LEAD automatically)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/clients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Alex",
  "lastName": "Smith",
  "email": "alex@example.com",
  "phone": "+19876543210",
  "companyName": "Smith Technologies",
  "address": "New York",
  "clientType": "BUSINESS",
  "notes": "Interested in website development"
}

### List clients with search and filters
GET http://localhost:8080/api/clients?search=alex&status=ACTIVE&clientType=BUSINESS

### Client summary
GET http://localhost:8080/api/clients/REPLACE_WITH_REAL_CLIENT_ID/summary

### Create a project (a LEAD client becomes ACTIVE)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Company Website",
  "description": "Build a responsive company website",
  "clientId": "REPLACE_WITH_REAL_CLIENT_ID",
  "status": "PLANNED",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "startDate": "2026-10-16",
  "dueDate": "2026-12-20",
  "budget": 2500.00
}

### Overdue projects
GET http://localhost:8080/api/projects/overdue

### Projects filtered by status and priority
GET http://localhost:8080/api/projects?status=IN_PROGRESS&priority=HIGH

### Projects of one client
GET http://localhost:8080/api/clients/REPLACE_WITH_REAL_CLIENT_ID/projects

### Add an interaction
POST http://localhost:8080/api/clients/REPLACE_WITH_REAL_CLIENT_ID/interactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "MEETING",
  "subject": "Initial requirements discussion",
  "description": "Discussed the client's website requirements.",
  "interactionDate": "2026-10-16"
}

### Interaction history (newest first)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/clients/REPLACE_WITH_REAL_CLIENT_ID/interactions

### Dashboard statistics
GET http://localhost:8080/api/dashboard/summary
